# bazas-proxy is in DECOMMISSION mode

This repository is a **dumb HTTP forwarder** that forwards external vendor
webhooks (VAPI, Zapier, Thumbtack) to `crm.asap.repair`. It exists ONLY because
those vendor dashboards have hard-coded URLs pointing here that we cannot change
instantly.

## Hard rules

1. **NEVER add business logic, AI calls, database access, or third-party
   integrations to this repo.** Add them to `bazas-crm` instead.
2. **NEVER modify** `api/vapi.legacy.js` — it is a frozen reference of the
   pre-decommission implementation kept only for emergency rollback.
3. The ONLY legitimate edits here are:
   - Adding a new forwarder route (one-liner using `forwardToCrm` from `lib/forwarder.js`)
   - Removing a forwarder once the corresponding vendor URL has been migrated off
   - Bumping `FORWARD_TARGET_BASE` env var

## Where to actually go

| Topic | Repository |
|-------|-----------|
| Anything VAPI / voice / phone | `bazas-crm/app/api/vapi/*`, `bazas-crm/app/api/twilio/*` |
| Anything Yelp / Thumbtack / Google LSA / Email leads | `bazas-crm/app/api/webhooks/*` |
| Website widgets / quote form | `bazas-crm/app/api/widget/*` |
| Calendar / appointments | `bazas-crm/app/api/calendar/*` |
| Knowledge base / pricing | `bazas-crm/lib/knowledge-base*` and Settings UI |
| AI auto-reply / Judge rules | `bazas-crm/app/api/ai/*` |
| Telegram notifications | `bazas-crm/lib/telegram-notify.ts` |
| Frontend / static site | `asap.repair/` (Cloudflare Pages) |

## If you think you need to debug something here

99% of the time, you don't. The forwarder is ~100 lines of deterministic
HTTP-passthrough. If a vendor webhook is broken, the bug is almost certainly
in the corresponding CRM route, not here.

To verify, hit both URLs with curl and compare responses:

```bash
curl -X POST https://repair-asap-proxy-production.up.railway.app/api/vapi/webhook -d '...'
curl -X POST https://crm.asap.repair/api/vapi/webhook -d '...'
```

If responses match → the bug is in `bazas-crm`. Stop reading code here, switch
repositories.
